Use macOS-style key bindings (Meta+C/Z/A..., Ctrl+click as secondary click) only
with the macOS GDK backend, not on every Apple build. With only the Wayland
backend on Darwin, apps get the standard Linux bindings (Ctrl+C, Ctrl+Z), and
Cmd stays free for the compositor (see docs/decisions.md).

--- a/gdk/gdkevents.c
+++ b/gdk/gdkevents.c
@@ -998,7 +998,7 @@
